zurngtest bundles PractRand 0.96, by Chris Doty-Humphrey, in src/practrand/.

PractRand is released to the public domain, with the Creative Commons CC0
1.0 Universal dedication as a fallback where a public-domain dedication is
not recognised. Its notice is src/practrand/LICENSE. That notice also covers
the generators PractRand includes: jsf and isaac were designed by Robert
Jenkins, who released them to the public domain; the hc256 implementation
starts from the eSTREAM reference implementation, whose authors made the
cipher free for anyone to use; the remaining implementations are Chris
Doty-Humphrey's own.

The "NotRecommended" generators upstream ships in RNGs/other/ are not
bundled, because the notice says some of that code was copied from public
sources without a stated licence.

src/practrand/ is upstream's library plus two local patches, described in
src/practrand/PROVENANCE: one removes output to stdout and stderr and calls
to exit(), the other fixes compiler warnings.

